as the walking dead slowly works its way  to its inevitable conclusion  after 11 seasons the 10th season episode  find me goes back to the past if you  aren't caught up on the walking dead  there are spoilers ahead dead fans got a  blast to the past in the latest episode  of season 10  which begins with daryl carol and dog  heading out together on a scouting trip  where daryl is confronted by difficult  memories of a very special woman  the episode not only gives fans a look  at what the upcoming daryl and carol  spin-off series might look like but it  also provides a look into the lost years  after rick's disappearance the setup of  the episode is simple enough  carol talks herself into tagging along  with daryl on his expedition which  takes them deep into the woods  surrounding alexandria it's clear that  things  aren't right even though their community  prevailed in the whisperer war  they did so at an incredible cost carol  brings up the destruction of hilltop and  the sacking of alexandria  our luck's run out daryl isn't  in the mood to chat but he's forced to  open up when the pair come across an  abandoned cabin in the woods  while searching the cabin carol finds a  hidden compartment in the floor that  contains some hidden food  and a note written by daryl it's clear  that he has some history with this place  at carol's request he fills her in on  what happened to him there  daryl's story begins during the period  after rick was seemingly killed in a  bridge explosion  we already learned in season 9 that  daryl spent several years after that  event  living in the woods and searching for  any sign of rick this is what we see him  doing and find me  carefully marking locations on a map  he's living in a makeshift  camp and scouring the area for rick's  body when he meets a small  dog who turns out to be none other than  dog  daryl's eventual canine companion they  part ways but dog makes  many trips back to daryl one day dog  runs up to daryl and starts barking for  him to follow  which leads them to an isolated cabin in  the woods with  some walkers inside after daryl  eliminates the threat a woman with a gun  bursts  out of a bedroom she ties daryl up and  interrogates him about who he is and why  he's in her house  once she's convinced that he's not a  genuine threat  she lets him go but makes it clear she  doesn't want to see him on her  property again daryl and the woman  who eventually reveals that her name is  leah begin having a series of run-ins  where one  helps the other but because both of them  are extremely independent  neither seem too happy about it first  leah gives daryl a hand when he finds  himself surrounded by a pack of walkers  only for him to tell her  then daryl catches a fish and leaves it  on leah's porch which she returns  neither can let their guard down long  enough to become vulnerable to the other  that all changes when leah finds daryl  out in the cold and convinces him to  come back to her cabin  while he's there she reveals that it's  her adopted son's birthday and explains  to daryl that she has no  actual family of her own but formed a  close  familial bond with her military squadron  leah tells daryl about the day that a  horde of walkers attacked her group and  she lost her entire adopted family daryl  in turn tells her about rick the knight  of vulnerability softens both of them  and daryl ends up coming to live in  leah's cabin  unfortunately it isn't meant to last  even after daryl moves in with leah he  can't abandon his mission to find  evidence of what happened to rick which  puts a strain on their budding romantic  relationship  leah is clearly someone who has a hard  time letting people into her life  losing her son and her family was a  profoundly traumatic moment  and she had a hard time watching daryl  leave when daryl tells leah he'll be  gone for a few days  she doesn't take that news well where do  you belong daryl  out there in the river looking for your  dead brother day after day after day  or do you belong here with me when daryl  responds that he doesn't  know she challenges him to make a choice  daryl goes on his trip but he has the  revelation that he wants to be with leah  instead  when he returns to the cabin she's gone  and there are no  obvious clues as to what happened to her  he leaves her a note in her secret stash  of food that reads  i belong with you find me this is the  note that carol discovers in the present  day  a sad indication that leah never ended  up returning to her cabin between then  and now  and what happened to her is a mystery  it's not likely that daryl will get a  happy ending with her however  considering daryl and carol have an  entire spin-off series to embark on  while daryl and his relationship with  leah is the primary focus of find me  the episode also puts the spotlight on  daryl and carol's bond  during daryl's long time away in the  woods carol comes to meet with him  multiple times  often expressing worry that their  community is in danger of falling apart  she also tries to gently persuade daryl  to rejoin them in alexandria he  eventually does  but during the flashbacks he mostly  turns a cold shoulder to carol  in the present day when carol tries to  implore  daryl to not blame himself for leah's  disappearance he  lashes out at her he accuses carol of  trying to get him wrapped up in her own  personal issues  carol says that the only thing she's  asking of him  is friendship daryl is pushing carol  away to avoid vulnerability the same as  we saw him do to leah during the  flashback sequences  the difference is that he and carol are  old friends who have been through  a lot together so it's devastating to  see them break down like this  i was right  her looks run out you and me fortunately  there's still plenty of time for carol  and daryl to mend their friendship and  become  the strong resilient duo fans know them  to be  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the walking dead are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  [Music]  you
 

